ormat="epo"><addressbook><name>ITOH KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATSURA TAKATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUNAMI YOSHINORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MOCHIZUKI MITSURU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGANO HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUYAMA, SHINJIROU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI, RYOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIZU, FUMIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITOH, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATSURA, TAKATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNAMI, YOSHINORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOCHIZUKI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGANO, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A logarithmic amplifier (11) having a large input range first detects the level of the baseband signal on the input side of a variable gain amplifier circuit (8). Based on the detected level, a control section (13) performs coarse feedfoward control of the gain of the variable gain amplifier circuit (8). A root-mean-square circuit (14) determines the output level of an A/D converter (10) and supplies it to the control section (13). Based on the detected level, the control section (13) performs fine feedback control of the variable gain amplifier (8).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Dans la présente invention, un amplificateur logarithmique (11) ayant une large plage d'entrée détecte tout d'abord le niveau du signal de bande de base du côté entrée d'un circuit (8) d'amplificateur à gain variable. Sur la base du niveau détecté, une partie de commande (13) effectue la commande de correction prédictive forte du gain du circuit (8) d'amplificateur à gain variable. Un circuit (14) de moyenne quadratique détermine le niveau de sortie d'un convertisseur A/N (10) et l'envoie à la partie de commande (13). Sur la base du niveau détecté, la partie de commande (13) effectue la commande de rétroaction fine de l'amplificateur (8) à gain variable.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>